            <ArticleTitle>Giant rhinophyma in a bronchial asthma patient treated by excision and full thickness skin grafting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 72-year-old man presented with an unusually severe case of rhinophyma. The pedunculated mass was widely excised and a skin graft from the medial upper arm was applied. A very satisfactory cosmetic result was obtained.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
